%S A397101 1,1,1,1,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,10,13,17,22,28,35,43,52,62,73,86,102,122,147,
%T A397101 178,216,262,317,382,458,546,647,762,893,1043,1216,1417,1652,1928,
%U A397101 2253,2636,3087,3617,4238,4963,5806,6782,7907,9198,10674,12357,14273,16453
%N A397101 Number of compositions (c_1,...,c_k) of n with c_i >= 2*k - i.
%C A397101 Equivalently, the number of compositions from whose bargraph the staircase (k-1, k-2, ..., 1, 0) can be subtracted twice with a superdiagonal composition remaining, where a composition (c_1,...,c_k) is superdiagonal if c_i >= i for all i.
%C A397101 The minimal weight of a length-k composition of this type is the k-th pentagonal number k*(3*k-1)/2. This is the r = 2 member of a hierarchy in which the length-k minimal weight is the k-th (r+3)-gonal number: r = 0 gives A219282 (triangular numbers) and r = 1 gives A098131 (square numbers).
%H A397101 Mohammad F. Marashdeh, <a href="/A397101/b397101.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%F A397101 a(n) = Sum_{k>=1, k*(3*k-1)/2 <= n} binomial(n-1-3*k*(k-1)/2, k-1) for n >= 1; a(0) = 1.
%F A397101 G.f.: Sum_{k>=0} x^(k*(3*k-1)/2) / (1-x)^k.
%e A397101 a(5) = 2: the length-1 composition [5], and the length-2 composition [3,2], whose lower bounds 2*k-i are (3,2).
%o A397101 (PARI) a(n) = if(n==0, 1, sum(k=1, n, binomial(max(n-1-3*k*(k-1)/2, 0), k-1)));
%Y A397101 Cf. A219282, A098131, A397066, A236310.
%K A397101 nonn
%O A397101 0,6
%A A397101 _Mohammad F. Marashdeh_, Jul 15 2026
